          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              \-symmetry
            in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            is a certain fermionic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functionals"} Green-Schwarz action functionals
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-branes"} super p-branes
            whose effect is to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+symmetry"} gauge away
            half of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor"} spinorial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
          %h2#as_superdiffeomorphisms_in_the_superembedding_approach As super-diffeomorphisms in the super-embedding approach
          %p
            In a completely super-covariant formulation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functionals"} Green-Schwarz action functionals
            – called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-embedding+formalism"} super-embedding formalism
            – this
            = succeed "-symmetry" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} super
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-diffeomorphism"} super-diffeomorphism
            symmetry of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            (
            %a{:href => "#SorokinTkachVolkov89"}> Sorokin-Tkach-Volkov 89
            , review includes
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sorokin99"} Sorokin 99, section 4.3
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#HoweSezgin04"} Howe-Sezgin 04, section 4.3
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                denotes a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetime"} superspacetime
                locally modeled on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Minkowski+spacetime"} super-Minkowski spacetime
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                denotes a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} super
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super p-brane
                locally modeled on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Minkowski+spacetime"} super-Minkowski spacetime
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p,1\vert \mathbf{N}/2}
            %li
              %p
                so that a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
                configuration for a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super p-brane
                of shape
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                to popagate in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a morphism of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifolds"} supermanifolds
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Σ
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mtext super-worldvolume
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi ϕ
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mtext sigma-model super-field
                            %mtd
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mtext super-spacetime
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\Sigma &amp;&amp; \text{super-worldvolume}
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi}} &amp;&amp;\text{sigma-model super-field}&amp;
                      \\\
                      X &amp;&amp; \text{super-spacetime}
                      }
          %p then:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the postcomposition
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-isometries"} super-isometries
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ≃
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} X
                is in even degree the action of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometries"} isometries
                and in odd degree the action of
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
                on the sigma-model fields;
            %li
              %p
                the precomposition action of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-diffeomorphism"} super-diffeomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \Sigma
                is in even degree the action of bosonic worldvolume
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
                and in odd degree the action of
                = succeed ":" do
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi κ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                    \-symmetry
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                        %mtd
                          %munderover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ≃
                            %mrow
                              %mi κ
                              %mtext -symmetry
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi ϕ
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mo ′
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %munderover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ≃
                            %mtext spacetime supersymmetry
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\Sigma  &amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{\kappa\text{-symmetry}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Sigma
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi'}}
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{\text{spacetime supersymmetry}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  X
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice here the assumption that the number of odd directions on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            is half that of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-branes"} super p-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            solutions are
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
          %p For example, consider the embedding
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^{2,1} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{10,1}
          %p
            of 2+1d
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane"} membrane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{10,1}
            from the 11d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+group"} Poincaré group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso(10,1)
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+group"} product group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Iso(2,1) \times SO(8)
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  Iso(10,1)
          %p
            (meaning that this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+subgroup"} stabilizer subgroup
            of the embedding).
          %p
            Now consider instead
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}}
            (with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
            the irreducible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinor"} Majorana spinor
            representation in 11), hence the local model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetimes"} super spacetimes
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
            preserves the embedding in that the
            %a{:href => "Majorana+spinor#TheSpinorPairingToVectors"} spinor bilinear pairing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mn 1
                  %mi Γ
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\psi}_1 \Gamma \psi_2
            on that subspace lands in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{2,1} \hookrightarrow Iso(2,1) \hookrightarrow Iso(10,1)
            (
            %a{:href => "#Sorokin99"}> Sorokin 99, section 5.1
            ). This is found to be the case for a half-dimensional subspace, and hence we may lift the above to a super-embedding of the form
          #eq:M2WordvolumeInSpacetime.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 8
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert 8 \otimes \mathbf{2}} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}}
          %p
            (where now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irrep"} irreducible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinor"} Majorana spinor
            representation in 3d, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 8
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 8 \otimes \mathbf{2}
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of 8 copies of it) such that the induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+group"} stabilizer
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
            inside the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} super Poincaré group
            now is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 8
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 32
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Iso(\mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert 8 \otimes \mathbf{2}}) \times Spin(8)
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  Iso(\mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}})
                  \\,.
          %p
            It is in this sense that the membrane “breaks exactly half the supersymmetry”, namely from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 8
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 8 \otimes \mathbf{2}
          %p
            If one now thinks of this not as inclusions of global spacetimes, but of their super tangent spaces at the points where the membrane sits in spacetime, then this reflects the local structure of
            = succeed "-symmetry:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-symmetries" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Iso
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 8
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso(\mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert 8 \otimes \mathbf{2}} )
          %p
            This explains why
            = succeed "-symmetry" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+models"} Green-Schwarz sigma models
            is taken to quotient out precisely half the spinor components, hence why, in the fully super-covariant formulation, one takes the worldvolume of a super
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
            to be
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p,1\vert \mathbf{N}/2}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+models"} sigma models
            for “non-BPS super
            = succeed "-branes\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %h2#history History
          %p
            Historically
            = succeed "-symmetry" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+models"} Green-Schwarz sigma models
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            is regarded as an ordinary (bosonic)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "-symmetry" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-particle"} super-particle
            (
            %a{:href => "#AzcarragLukierski82"}> Azcarraga-Lukierski 82
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Siegel83"} Siegel 83
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+1-brane+in+3d"} super 1-brane in 3d
            (
            %a{:href => "#Siegel84"}> Siegel 84
            ).
          %p
            Based on this the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            in 10d (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"}> heterotic string
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring"} type II superstring
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GreenSchwarz84"} Green-Schwarz 84
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nambu-Goto+action"} Nambu-Goto action
            for a string on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            has twice as many fermionic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} on-shell
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degrees+of+freedom"} degrees of freedom
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NSR-string"} NSR-string
            and then by adding a term to the action (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW-term"} WZW-term
            = succeed "-symmetry." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-symmetric" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            actions for all the other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-branes"} super p-branes
            were found, for instance for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            in (
            %a{:href => "#BergshoeffSezginTownsend87"}> Bergshoeff-Sezgin-Townsend 87
            ).
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+supersymmetry"} geometry of physics – supersymmetry
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Originally,
            = succeed "-symmetry" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-particle"} super-particle
            in
          %ul
            %li#AzcarragaLukierski82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"}> J. de Azcárraga
                , J. Lukierski,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetric particles
            %li#Siegel83
              %p
                Warren Siegel,
                %em Hidden Local Supersymmetry In The Supersymmetric Particle Action
                Phys. Lett. B 128, 397 (1983)
          %p
            and for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+1-brane+in+3d"} super 1-brane in 3d
            in
          %ul
            %li#Siegel84
              Warren Siegel,
              %em Light Cone Analysis Of Covariant Superstring
              , Nucl. Phys. B 236, 311 (1984).
          %p
            Then it was used to define/construct the manifestly spacetime supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            in 10d in
          %ul
            %li#GreenSchwarz84
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
              = succeed "," do
                %em Covariant description of superstrings
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1984PhLB..136..367G"} web
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/193596"} spire:193596
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(84)92021-5"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(84)92021-5
          %p
            and then for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            in 11d in
          %ul
            %li#BergshoeffSezginTownsend87
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Bergshoeff"}> Eric Bergshoeff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em Supermembranes and eleven-dimensional supergravity
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://streaming.ictp.trieste.it/preprints/P/87/010.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and so forth (see the references at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super p-brane
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} super-geometric
            interpretation of
            = succeed "-symmetry" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-diffeomorphism"} super-diffeomorphism
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super p-brane
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            was first suggested in
          %ul
            %li#SorokinTkachVolkov89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Sorokin"}> Dmitri Sorokin
              , V. Tkach and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitrij+Volkov"} Dmitrij Volkov
              = succeed "," do
                %em Superparticles, twistors and Siegel symmetry
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/271923"} spire:271923
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217732389001064"} doi:10.1142/S0217732389001064
          %p Review of this perspective includes
          %ul
            %li#Sorokin99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Sorokin"}> Dmitri Sorokin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superbranes and Superembeddings
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9906142"} arXiv:hep-th/9906142
            %li#HoweSezgin04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"}> Paul Howe
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The supermembrane revisited
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0412245"} arXiv:hep-th/0412245
